{"kind":"project","sections":[{"backgroundImage":"ch_thumbnail.png","kind":"hero","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26 or later","estimatedTimeInMinutes":15,"projectFiles":"OvertheCloud-Assets.zip","title":"Set up the project and assets","image":"ch_thumbnail.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This tutorial uses a sky texture in the app bundle and cloud models in a local Swift package. Download and extract ","type":"text"},{"code":"OvertheCloud-Assets.zip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Project files"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" below, then connect the texture to the app target and add the package as a dependency.","type":"text"}]}],"chapter":"1. Set up the project and assets"},{"tasks":[{"title":"Create a visionOS app and download the assets","contentSection":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following steps assume a new SwiftUI visionOS app. You can also use an existing project, but set its minimum deployment target to visionOS 26 or later to match the supplied "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloudpractice"},{"type":"text","text":" package."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"stepsSection":[{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_1_create.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Xcode, choose "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"File ▸ New ▸ Project ▸ visionOS ▸ App","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to create a visionOS app."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_2_create_name.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set the product name to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OvertheCloud"},{"type":"text","text":". Using the same name keeps file names and target selections consistent with the examples that follow."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_3_files.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tutorial provides the sky texture and cloud models. Download "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OvertheCloud-Assets.zip"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Project files","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and extract it to find the sky texture, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"skyBg_ASTC.ktx"},{"type":"text","text":", and the local Swift package, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloudpractice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The code locates assets by their file names and entity names. Keep the supplied names and folder structure unchanged.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"}]}],"anchor":"Create-a-visionOS-app-and-download-the-assets"},{"title":"Add the sky texture and cloud models to Xcode","contentSection":[{"media":"ch1_4_start.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sky texture belongs in the main app bundle. The cloud models belong to the separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloudpractice"},{"type":"text","text":" module. Both connections are required for asset preloading to succeed."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"stepsSection":[{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_5_add.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"skyBg_ASTC.ktx"},{"type":"text","text":" into the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OvertheCloud"},{"type":"text","text":" app group in the Xcode project navigator to include the sky texture in the app."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_5.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Copying the file into the project and adding it to the app target lets the app load the sky without relying on the original file location. In the sheet, select "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Copy files to destination","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OvertheCloud"},{"type":"text","text":" target, then choose "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Finish","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_6_skyimg.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target Membership","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" determines which app includes the texture. Select "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OvertheCloud"},{"type":"text","text":" in the File inspector so the running app can find the texture in its bundle."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_7_pkg.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The downloaded "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloudpractice"},{"type":"text","text":" package provides the cloud models and their resource bundle. Choose "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"File ▸ Add Package Dependencies ▸ Add Local","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", then select the extracted "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloudpractice"},{"type":"text","text":" folder to make those assets available to the app."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_8_pkg2.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Connecting the package to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OvertheCloud"},{"type":"text","text":" app target makes the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloudpractice"},{"type":"text","text":" module and its assets available in code. Later, the app uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cloud_A"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cloud_B"},{"type":"text","text":" to create clouds with different shapes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"code":null,"type":"step","media":"ch1_9_fin.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirm that the sky texture appears in the project navigator and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloudpractice"},{"type":"text","text":" appears under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Package Dependencies","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Both must be available before the cache can load the sky and clouds."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If Xcode reports ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"No such module"},{"text":", check that the package is connected to the app target. If the texture cannot be found, check its file name and Target Membership.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"}]}],"anchor":"Add-the-sky-texture-and-cloud-models-to-Xcode"}],"kind":"tasks"},{"abstract":[{"text":"A window and an immersive view need shared state to coordinate their behavior. Create an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that uses the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro to represent the state of the immersive space.","type":"text"}],"action":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter1-AppModel","overridingTitle":"Get started","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}],"isActive":true,"type":"reference"},"kind":"callToAction","title":"Model the app state","featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/2026techmap_tutorial\/chapter0-setup"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter0-Setup","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial","doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/$volume","